/* Original fictional readings. Every source sentence is prepared before whole-text practice. */
(()=>{'use strict';
const lt=LANG.code==='lt';
const rows=lt?[
['B1-community','The Saturday that changed our plan','narrative',
[
['A plan on paper',[
['Pirmą kartą padėjau rengti mūsų rajono knygų šventę, todėl iš pradžių norėjau turėti labai aiškų planą.','I was helping organise our neighbourhood book event for the first time, so initially I wanted a very clear plan.'],
['Su Lina sutarėme, kad šeštadienį stalus pastatysime kieme, o savanoriai ateis devintą valandą, prieš atvykstant lankytojams.','Lina and I agreed to put the tables in the courtyard on Saturday, with volunteers coming at nine before visitors arrived.'],
['Mokytoja pažadėjo atsivesti savo mokinius, kaimynas pasiūlė atnešti senų knygų, o aš turėjau parengti trumpą skelbimą.','A teacher promised to bring her pupils, a neighbour offered old books, and I was to prepare a short notice.'],
['Atrodė, kad visi žino savo darbus, tačiau penktadienio vakarą supratau, kad skelbime parašėme tik vietą ir pradžios laiką.','Everyone seemed to know their jobs, but on Friday evening I realised our notice gave only the place and starting time.'],
['Nebuvome parašę, ar knygas galima tik pirkti, ar žmonės taip pat galės jomis keistis ir tiesiog ateiti pasikalbėti.','We had not said whether books could only be bought or whether people could also exchange them and simply come to talk.']]],
['Rain and a locked door',[
['Šeštadienio rytą stipriai lijo, todėl Lina pasiūlė šventę perkelti į bendruomenės salę, esančią kitame to paties pastato gale.','It rained heavily on Saturday morning, so Lina proposed moving the event to the community hall at the other end of the same building.'],
['Salė buvo laisva, bet žmogus, kuris turėjo jos raktą, galėjo atvykti tik pusę dešimtos.','The hall was free, but the person with its key could arrive only at half past nine.'],
['Vienas savanoris norėjo iš karto viską atšaukti, nes bijojo, kad prie užrakintų durų susirinkę lankytojai supyks.','One volunteer wanted to cancel immediately because he feared visitors gathering at the locked doors would be angry.'],
['Paprašiau jo pirmiausia paskambinti mokytojai, o pati nuėjau prie kiemo vartų pasitikti anksčiau atėjusių žmonių.','I asked him first to call the teacher, while I went to the courtyard gate to meet people arriving early.'],
['Paaiškinau, kodėl keičiame vietą, ir pasakiau, kad šventė prasidės pusvalandžiu vėliau, bet tikrai įvyks.','I explained why we were changing the location and said the event would start half an hour later but would definitely take place.']]],
['A different kind of help',[
['Laukdami rakto pamatėme, kad prie pagrindinio įėjimo yra laiptai, kuriais vienai lankytojai su vežimėliu būtų sunku pakilti.','While waiting for the key, we noticed steps at the main entrance that would be difficult for a visitor with a pushchair.'],
['Kaimynas žinojo kitą įėjimą be laiptų, tačiau iki jo reikėjo apeiti pastatą ir niekur nebuvo rodyklės.','A neighbour knew another entrance without steps, but reaching it meant walking around the building and there was no sign.'],
['Užuot iš karto nešę knygų dėžes, du savanoriai padarė aiškias rodykles ir vieną žmogų paliko prie vartų.','Instead of immediately carrying book boxes, two volunteers made clear signs and left one person at the gate.'],
['Mokytoja su mokiniais atėjo vėliau, todėl niekam nereikėjo ilgai stovėti lietuje, o laukę kaimynai padėjo sustatyti stalus.','The teacher and pupils arrived later, so nobody had to stand in the rain for long, and neighbours who had waited helped arrange tables.'],
['Tada supratau, kad svarbiausias darbas kartais yra ne tas, kurį iš anksto įrašai į savo sąrašą.','Then I understood that sometimes the most important job is not the one you put on your list beforehand.']]],
['What we wrote afterwards',[
['Po šventės suskaičiavome knygas ir pamatėme, kad jų išdalijome mažiau, negu tikėjomės, nors žmonių atėjo nemažai.','After the event we counted the books and found we had given away fewer than expected, although quite a few people came.'],
['Tačiau keli lankytojai pasakė, kad pirmą kartą susipažino su savo kaimynais, o mokiniai paprašė panašaus renginio kitą mėnesį.','But several visitors said they had met their neighbours for the first time, and pupils requested a similar event next month.'],
['Todėl savo ataskaitoje parašėme ne tik knygų skaičių, bet ir tai, ko žmonėms reikėjo ir kas jiems patiko.','Our report therefore included not just the number of books, but also what people needed and enjoyed.'],
['Kitą kartą iš anksto patikrinsime raktą, prieinamą įėjimą ir pranešime, kaip elgsimės, jeigu vėl lis.','Next time we will check the key and accessible entrance beforehand and explain what we will do if it rains again.'],
['Dabar vis dar mėgstu aiškų planą, bet žinau, kad geras planas turi palikti vietos pokalbiui ir pokyčiams.','I still like a clear plan, but now know a good plan must leave room for conversation and changes.']]]],
['A notice should explain the purpose, not just the time.','A delay could be managed without cancelling the event.','Making the entrance usable mattered more than moving boxes first.','The final judgement used more than the book total.']],
['B2-media','The headline and the missing comparison','reported argument',
[
['A striking number',[
['Vietos laikraštis paskelbė, kad po naujos skaityklos atidarymo bibliotekos lankytojų skaičius išaugo trečdaliu, ir antraštėje pavadino pokytį neabejotina sėkme.','A local newspaper reported a one-third increase in library visits after a new reading room opened, calling the change an unquestionable success in its headline.'],
['Straipsnyje buvo cituojama bibliotekos vadovė, kuri džiaugėsi galėdama pasiūlyti daugiau vietų mokiniams ir žmonėms, dirbantiems ne namuose.','The article quoted the library director welcoming more places for pupils and people working away from home.'],
['Naujos erdvės iš tiesų buvo pilnos, tačiau skaitytoja Rasa pastebėjo, kad nenurodyta, su kuriuo laikotarpiu lyginamas dabartinis lankomumas.','The new spaces really were full, but reader Rasa noticed that the period used for comparison was not stated.'],
['Jai rūpėjo ne paneigti pagerėjimą, o suprasti, ar skaičius leidžia spręsti būtent apie skaityklos poveikį.','She wanted not to deny improvement but to understand whether the figure specifically demonstrated the reading room’s effect.']]],
['A comparison that changed the story',[
['Paprašyta paaiškinimo, biblioteka pateikė mėnesio duomenis ir patvirtino, kad ankstesniais metais tuo pačiu metu pastatas dvi savaites buvo remontuojamas.','Asked for clarification, the library supplied monthly data and confirmed the building had been under repair for two weeks during the corresponding period the year before.'],
['Taigi naujas skaičius buvo lyginamas su mėnesiu, kai lankytojai negalėjo naudotis visomis įprastomis paslaugomis.','The new figure was therefore compared with a month when visitors could not use all the usual services.'],
['Be to, šiemet biblioteka šeštadieniais dirbo ilgiau, o mokykla šalia jos laikinai uždarė savo skaitymo kambarį.','This year the library also opened longer on Saturdays, and a nearby school temporarily closed its reading room.'],
['Šios aplinkybės nereiškė, kad naujoji skaitykla nereikalinga, bet neleido viso augimo patikimai priskirti vien jos atidarymui.','These circumstances did not mean the new reading room was unnecessary, but prevented reliably attributing the entire increase to its opening alone.']]],
['Two useful objections',[
['Vadovė atsakė, kad darbuotojai kasdien mato daugiau besimokančių žmonių ir gauna gerų atsiliepimų, todėl vien statistikos trūkumais sėkmės vertinti nereikėtų.','The director replied that staff saw more people studying daily and received positive feedback, so statistical shortcomings alone should not determine the judgement.'],
['Rasa sutiko, jog lankytojų patirtis svarbi, tačiau priminė, kad dažniausiai atsiliepia tie, kurie jau naudojasi paslauga.','Rasa agreed that visitor experience mattered but noted that feedback usually came from people already using the service.'],
['Žmonės, kuriems naujos darbo valandos netinka arba kuriems sunku atvykti, tokiame pasakojime gali likti beveik nematomi.','People unable to use the new hours or reach the library might remain almost invisible in such an account.'],
['Abi pusės galėjo būti teisios dėl skirtingų dalykų: darbuotojų patirtis rodė poreikį, o palyginimo ribotumas silpnino konkretų priežastinį teiginį.','Both sides could be right about different things: staff experience indicated demand, while the limited comparison weakened the specific causal claim.']]],
['A correction with a purpose',[
['Laikraštis vėliau papildė straipsnį paaiškinimu apie remontą ir pakeitė antraštę, tačiau pirminė žinutė socialiniuose tinkluose jau buvo plačiai pasidalyta.','The newspaper later added an explanation about the repairs and changed the headline, but the original social-media message had already been widely shared.'],
['Redakcija nusprendė pataisymą paskelbti tose pačiose paskyrose, užuot tik tyliai pakeitusi tekstą savo svetainėje.','The editors decided to publish the correction on the same accounts rather than silently changing only the website text.'],
['Kitam vertinimui pasiūlyta lyginti panašias savaites, atsižvelgti į darbo valandas ir paklausti ne tik nuolatinių lankytojų.','The next evaluation would compare similar weeks, take opening hours into account and ask more than regular visitors.'],
['Tikslesnė išvada buvo santūresnė, bet naudingesnė: erdvė naudojama, o jos atskirą poveikį dar reikės įvertinti geresniais duomenimis.','The more precise conclusion was more restrained but useful: the space was being used, while its separate effect still needed evaluation with better data.']]]],
['A true count does not automatically support the headline’s causal claim.','A fair comparison needs comparable access and opening hours.','Positive experiences and weak causal evidence can coexist.','A correction should reach the audience that saw the original claim.']],
['C1-academic','Two explanations for an apparent improvement','analytical case study',
[
['The question behind the result',[
['Universiteto darbo grupė norėjo išsiaiškinti, ar ilgesnis bibliotekos darbo laikas padeda studentams reguliariau dalyvauti savarankiško mokymosi grupėse.','A university working group wanted to establish whether longer library hours helped students attend independent study groups more regularly.'],
['Po vieno semestro dalyvavimas vakarinėse grupėse padidėjo, tačiau ataskaitos autorė Ieva atsisakė šį pokytį iš karto vadinti naujo grafiko poveikiu.','After one semester evening-group attendance rose, but report author Ieva declined to immediately call this an effect of the new schedule.'],
['Tą patį semestrą pasikeitė ir užduočių pateikimo tvarka: dalį darbų studentai pirmiausia turėjo aptarti su bendramoksliais, o tik tada pateikti dėstytojui.','The assignment procedure changed that semester too: students first had to discuss some work with peers before submitting it to a lecturer.'],
['Todėl reikėjo atskirti du klausimus: ar patogesnis laikas palengvino dalyvavimą ir ar nauji reikalavimai sustiprino paskatą apskritai ateiti.','Two questions therefore needed separating: whether more convenient hours made attendance easier, and whether new requirements strengthened the incentive to attend at all.']]],
['What the comparisons could show',[
['Grupė palygino skirtingų studijų programų studentus, bet netrukus paaiškėjo, kad programos skiriasi ne vien naudojimosi biblioteka galimybėmis.','The group compared students on different programmes, but it soon became clear that the programmes differed in more than access to the library.'],
['Vienoje daugiau studentų dirbo vakarais, kitoje buvo daugiau privalomų bendrų užduočių, o kelionės išlaidos irgi pasiskirstė nevienodai.','More students worked evenings in one programme, another had more compulsory group assignments, and travel costs were also unevenly distributed.'],
['Paprastas vidurkių palyginimas galėjo aprašyti skirtumą, tačiau neatskleidė, kuri jo dalis susijusi su grafiku, o kuri su kitomis aplinkybėmis.','A simple comparison of averages could describe a difference but did not reveal how much was connected with the schedule and how much with other circumstances.'],
['Užuot ieškojusi vieno patogaus skaičiaus, Ieva pasiūlė aiškiai užrašyti alternatyvius paaiškinimus ir nurodyti, kokie papildomi stebėjimai padėtų juos atskirti.','Rather than seeking one convenient number, Ieva proposed explicitly recording alternative explanations and specifying additional observations that could distinguish them.']]],
['The interview that complicated the average',[
['Pokalbiuose keli studentai sakė, kad biblioteka jiems pagaliau tapo prieinama, nors bendras jų lankymosi dažnis per semestrą beveik nepasikeitė.','In interviews several students said the library had finally become accessible to them, even though their overall visit frequency barely changed that semester.'],
['Anksčiau jie atvykdavo rečiau ir pasilikdavo labai ilgai, o dabar galėjo rinktis trumpesnius susitikimus, geriau suderinamus su darbu ir šeimos pareigomis.','Previously they came less often and stayed a long time; now they could choose shorter meetings that fitted work and family responsibilities better.'],
['Kiti pripažino ateinantys daugiausia todėl, kad bendras aptarimas tapo užduoties dalimi; vien ilgesnės darbo valandos jų elgesio nebūtų pakeitusios.','Others acknowledged attending mainly because joint discussion had become part of the assignment; longer hours alone would not have changed their behaviour.'],
['Šie pasakojimai nepakeitė kiekybinių duomenų, bet parodė, kad tas pats rodiklis gali slėpti skirtingas patirtis ir skirtingus veikimo mechanizmus.','These accounts did not replace quantitative data, but showed that the same indicator could hide different experiences and different mechanisms.']]],
['A recommendation within the evidence',[
['Galutinėje rekomendacijoje grupė siūlė kitą semestrą išlaikyti dalį vakarinių valandų ir kartu sistemingai rinkti informaciją apie prieinamumą, užduotis bei dalyvavimo priežastis.','The final recommendation proposed retaining some evening hours next semester while systematically collecting information about access, assignments and reasons for attendance.'],
['Tai nebuvo nei pažadas, kad grafikas savaime pagerins mokymosi rezultatus, nei išvada, kad dabartiniai pokyčiai neturi vertės.','This was neither a promise that the schedule alone would improve learning outcomes nor a conclusion that current changes had no value.'],
['Sprendimas buvo grindžiamas matomu praktiniu poreikiu, o jo peržiūra turėjo priklausyti nuo aiškiai iš anksto įvardytų klausimų, ne vien nuo bendro pasitenkinimo.','The decision rested on a visible practical need, while its review would depend on questions specified beforehand, not just overall satisfaction.'],
['Ieva pabrėžė, kad atsargi išvada nėra tyrimo nesėkmė: ji leidžia veikti dabar ir kartu neapsimesti žinant daugiau, negu iš tikrųjų parodo surinkta medžiaga.','Ieva stressed that a cautious conclusion was not a research failure: it allowed action now without pretending the collected material showed more than it did.']]]],
['Separate easier access from a stronger incentive to attend.','A comparison can describe differences without isolating their cause.','An unchanged average may conceal a meaningful change in experience.','A provisional decision can be useful without an unsupported causal promise.']],
['C2-science','What the trial did not promise','qualified public explanation',
[
['A sentence that travelled',[
['Išgalvoto miesto aplinkos stebėjimo projekte buvo išbandyti nauji upės temperatūros jutikliai, o viešame pristatyme atsirado sakinys: sistema leidžia greičiau pastebėti pokyčius.','In a fictional city’s environmental monitoring project, new river-temperature sensors were trialled, and a public presentation stated that the system enabled changes to be noticed sooner.'],
['Techninėje ataskaitoje šis teiginys buvo siejamas su konkrečiomis bandymo sąlygomis, tačiau vėlesnėje santraukoje jis virto pažadu, kad upė nuo šiol bus nuolat ir patikimai stebima.','The technical report tied this statement to particular trial conditions, but a later summary turned it into a promise that the river would now be continuously and reliably monitored.'],
['Skirtumas atrodė nedidelis tik tol, kol nebuvo klausiama, ką skaitytojas pagrįstai supras žodžiu nuolat ir kas turės atsakyti, kai pranešimas nebus gautas.','The difference seemed small only until someone asked what a reader would reasonably understand by continuously and who would answer if no message arrived.'],
['Ataskaitos redaktorė nemanė, kad santraukos autorius sąmoningai klaidina: trumpindamas tekstą jis pašalino ne šalutinę detalę, o ribą, nuo kurios priklausė teiginio pagrįstumas.','The report’s editor did not assume intentional deception: in shortening the text, the summary writer had removed not a peripheral detail but a limit on which the claim’s validity depended.']]],
['The gaps in the record',[
['Bandymo metu numatyta šimtas matavimų, iš kurių devyniasdešimt keturi buvo gauti laiku, o šeši nepasiekė duomenų bazės dėl nutrūkusio ryšio.','The trial scheduled one hundred measurements; ninety-four arrived on time and six failed to reach the database because connectivity was interrupted.'],
['Iš gautų įrašų buvo galima vertinti veikimą tomis akimirkomis, kurioms turėta duomenų, bet trūkstami įrašai nepatvirtino nei temperatūros stabilumo, nei staigaus jos pokyčio.','Received records allowed evaluation at the moments for which data existed, but missing records confirmed neither stable temperature nor a sudden change.'],
['Vėliau atkurtos dalies įrašų nepakako spragai panaikinti, nes pristatymo pažadas buvo susijęs ne vien su galimybe kada nors sužinoti rezultatą, bet ir su jo gavimu laiku.','Recovering some records later did not remove the gap, because the presentation’s promise concerned not just eventually knowing a result but receiving it in time.'],
['Todėl teiginys, kad dauguma prietaisų veikė, ir teiginys, kad stebėjimas buvo nenutrūkstamas, negalėjo būti vartojami kaip lygiaverčiai, nors abu viešame pokalbyje skambėjo panašiai.','Thus a claim that most devices worked and a claim that monitoring was uninterrupted could not be treated as equivalent, although they sounded similar in public discussion.']]],
['Two objections that deserved different answers',[
['Gyventojų atstovė abejojo, ar verta tęsti projektą, jeigu negalima pažadėti nenutrūkstamo duomenų perdavimo, o projekto vadovas baiminosi, kad išsamus ribotumų sąrašas užgoš pasiektą pažangą.','A residents’ representative questioned continuing without a promise of uninterrupted transmission, while the project lead feared a detailed list of limitations would obscure progress.'],
['Redaktorė siūlė šių abejonių nesuplakti: pirmoji buvo susijusi su priimtina paslaugos riba, antroji su tuo, kaip apie ją kalbėti neprarandant nei tikslumo, nei prasmės.','The editor proposed keeping these concerns separate: the first concerned an acceptable service limit, the second how to communicate it without losing accuracy or meaning.'],
['Pažanga galėjo būti tikra ir kartu nepakankama tam tikram naudojimo būdui; pripažinus antrąją aplinkybę nereikėjo paneigti pirmosios ar nutylėti, kam sistema jau naudinga.','Progress could be real while insufficient for a particular use; acknowledging the latter did not require denying the former or concealing who already benefited.'],
['Vis dėlto žodžiai apie naudą neturėjo tapti pakaitalu atsakymui, kaip bus žymimos spragos, kas peržiūrės perspėjimus ir kokių išvadų vartotojas iš tylos daryti negali.','Nevertheless, statements of benefit could not replace an answer about marking gaps, reviewing alerts and conclusions a user must not draw from silence.']]],
['A shorter explanation that kept its limits',[
['Naujoje viešoje santraukoje buvo pasakyta, kad bandymo sąlygomis sistema suteikė daugiau laiku gautų stebėjimų, tačiau dalies matavimų perdavimas nutrūko ir tyla negali būti laikoma patvirtinimu, jog niekas nepasikeitė.','The revised public summary said the system supplied more timely observations under trial conditions, but transmission of some measurements failed and silence could not confirm that nothing changed.'],
['Techniniams naudotojams palikta atskira lentelė su gautais, pavėluotais ir negautais įrašais, o gyventojams paaiškinta, kur matyti ryšio būseną ir kam pranešti apie neatitikimą.','Technical users retained a separate table of received, late and missing records; residents were told where to see connection status and whom to notify about discrepancies.'],
['Sprendimas tęsti bandymą buvo susietas su patikrinamu veiksmu: prieš plečiant tinklą reikėjo išbandyti atsarginį perdavimą ir iš anksto nustatyti, kaip bus vertinamas vėlavimas.','Continuing the trial was tied to a verifiable action: test backup transmission before expanding the network and specify in advance how delay would be evaluated.'],
['Taip neapibrėžtumas liko matomas, bet netapo nei pretekstu viską atidėti, nei patogia išlyga, kuria būtų galima pateisinti bet kokį rezultatą po to, kai jis jau žinomas.','Uncertainty thus remained visible without becoming either a pretext for postponing everything or a convenient caveat used to justify any outcome once it was known.']]]],
['Preserve a condition that limits what the original claim warrants.','Missing or late data cannot be treated as timely evidence of stability.','Separate fitness for a purpose from how its limits should be communicated.','State a reviewable next step without promising certainty.']]
]:[
['B1-community','The Saturday that changed our plan','narrative',
[
['A plan on paper',[
['Era la primera vez que ayudaba a organizar una feria de libros en mi colonia y quería tener un plan muy claro.','It was my first time helping organise a book event in my neighbourhood, and I wanted a very clear plan.'],
['Mariana y yo acordamos poner las mesas en el patio el sábado; las personas voluntarias llegarían a las nueve, antes de recibir al público.','Mariana and I agreed to put the tables in the courtyard on Saturday; volunteers would arrive at nine before the public.'],
['Una maestra prometió llevar a su grupo, un vecino ofreció libros que ya no usaba y yo tenía que preparar un anuncio breve.','A teacher promised to bring her class, a neighbour offered books he no longer used, and I had to prepare a short notice.'],
['Parecía que cada quien sabía qué hacer, pero el viernes por la noche noté que el anuncio solamente decía el lugar y la hora.','Everyone seemed to know what to do, but on Friday night I noticed the notice gave only the place and time.'],
['No explicaba si había que comprar los libros, si se podían intercambiar o si también se podía ir nada más a platicar.','It did not explain whether books had to be bought, could be exchanged, or whether people could simply come to chat.']]],
['Rain and a locked door',[
['El sábado por la mañana llovía mucho y Mariana propuso mover la feria al salón comunitario, al otro lado del mismo edificio.','It rained heavily on Saturday morning and Mariana proposed moving the event to the community hall on the other side of the same building.'],
['El salón estaba libre, pero la persona que tenía la llave no podía llegar hasta las nueve y media.','The hall was free, but the person with the key could not arrive until half past nine.'],
['Un voluntario quería cancelar todo de inmediato porque le preocupaba que la gente se enojara al encontrar la puerta cerrada.','One volunteer wanted to cancel everything immediately because he worried people would be angry to find the door locked.'],
['Le pedí que primero llamara a la maestra y fui a la entrada del patio para recibir a quienes habían llegado temprano.','I asked him to call the teacher first and went to the courtyard entrance to receive people who had arrived early.'],
['Les expliqué el cambio y les dije que empezaríamos media hora más tarde, pero que sí habría feria.','I explained the change and said we would begin half an hour later but that the event would take place.']]],
['A different kind of help',[
['Mientras esperábamos la llave, vimos que la entrada principal tenía escalones y que sería difícil pasar por ahí con una carriola.','While waiting for the key, we saw steps at the main entrance that would make access with a pushchair difficult.'],
['Un vecino conocía otra entrada sin escalones, aunque para llegar había que rodear el edificio y no había ninguna señal.','A neighbour knew another entrance without steps, although reaching it meant going around the building and there were no signs.'],
['En vez de empezar por las cajas de libros, dos personas hicieron letreros claros y otra se quedó junto a la entrada del patio.','Instead of starting with the book boxes, two people made clear signs and another stayed at the courtyard entrance.'],
['La maestra llegó más tarde con su grupo y así nadie tuvo que esperar mucho bajo la lluvia; quienes ya estaban ayudaron con las mesas.','The teacher arrived later with her class so nobody had to wait long in the rain; people already there helped with tables.'],
['Entonces entendí que a veces el trabajo más importante no es el que habías escrito primero en tu lista.','Then I understood that sometimes the most important job is not the one you wrote first on your list.']]],
['What we wrote afterwards',[
['Al terminar contamos los libros y vimos que habíamos entregado menos de lo esperado, aunque sí había llegado bastante gente.','At the end we counted the books and found we had given away fewer than expected, although quite a few people had come.'],
['Sin embargo, varias personas dijeron que por primera vez habían conocido a sus vecinos y el grupo de la escuela pidió otra feria para el mes siguiente.','However, several people said they had met their neighbours for the first time, and the school group requested another event next month.'],
['Por eso nuestro informe incluyó tanto el número de libros como las necesidades y los comentarios de quienes participaron.','Our report therefore included both the book count and participants’ needs and comments.'],
['Para la próxima vez revisaremos antes la llave y la entrada accesible, y explicaremos qué pasará si vuelve a llover.','Next time we will check the key and accessible entrance beforehand and explain what will happen if it rains again.'],
['Todavía me gustan los planes claros, pero ahora sé que un buen plan también deja espacio para escuchar y cambiar.','I still like clear plans, but now know that a good plan also leaves room to listen and change.']]]],
['A notice should explain the purpose, not just the time.','A delay could be managed without cancelling the event.','Making the entrance usable mattered more than moving boxes first.','The final judgement used more than the book total.']],
['B2-media','The headline and the missing comparison','reported argument',
[
['A striking number',[
['Un periódico local informó que las visitas a la biblioteca habían aumentado una tercera parte después de abrir una nueva sala de lectura, y el titular presentó el cambio como un éxito indiscutible.','A local newspaper reported a one-third increase in library visits after a new reading room opened, and its headline presented this as an unquestionable success.'],
['La nota citaba a la directora, que celebraba poder ofrecer más lugares para estudiantes y para personas que trabajaban fuera de casa.','The report quoted the director welcoming more places for students and people working away from home.'],
['La nueva sala sí estaba llena, pero una lectora llamada Rosa notó que no se explicaba con qué periodo se comparaban las visitas actuales.','The new room really was full, but reader Rosa noticed that the comparison period for the current visits was not explained.'],
['Su intención no era negar la mejora, sino entender si ese número permitía atribuir el aumento específicamente a la nueva sala.','She did not want to deny improvement, but to understand whether the number allowed the increase to be attributed specifically to the new room.']]],
['A comparison that changed the story',[
['Cuando le pidieron una aclaración, la biblioteca compartió los datos del mes y confirmó que el año anterior el edificio había estado en reparación durante dos semanas del mismo periodo.','Asked for clarification, the library shared monthly data and confirmed that the building had been under repair for two weeks of the corresponding period the year before.'],
['Así, el número nuevo se comparaba con un mes en el que el público no había podido usar todos los servicios habituales.','The new number was thus compared with a month when the public could not use all the usual services.'],
['Además, ese año la biblioteca abría más horas los sábados y una escuela cercana había cerrado temporalmente su propio espacio de lectura.','The library also opened longer on Saturdays that year, and a nearby school had temporarily closed its reading space.'],
['Estas circunstancias no demostraban que la sala nueva fuera innecesaria, pero sí impedían atribuirle con confianza todo el crecimiento.','These circumstances did not show that the new room was unnecessary, but prevented confidently attributing all the growth to it.']]],
['Two useful objections',[
['La directora respondió que el personal veía a más personas estudiando todos los días y recibía comentarios positivos, por lo que no había que valorar el proyecto sólo por los problemas estadísticos.','The director replied that staff saw more people studying daily and received positive feedback, so statistical problems alone should not determine the project’s value.'],
['Rosa estuvo de acuerdo en que la experiencia importaba, pero recordó que los comentarios suelen venir de quienes ya usan el servicio.','Rosa agreed that experience mattered, but noted that comments usually came from people already using the service.'],
['Quienes no pueden llegar o tienen horarios incompatibles pueden quedar prácticamente fuera de ese relato, aunque sus necesidades también sean relevantes.','People unable to get there or with incompatible schedules can remain almost outside that account, although their needs also matter.'],
['Las dos partes podían tener razón sobre cosas distintas: la experiencia mostraba una necesidad y la comparación débil limitaba una afirmación concreta sobre sus causas.','Both sides could be right about different things: experience showed a need, while the weak comparison limited a particular causal claim.']]],
['A correction with a purpose',[
['El periódico añadió después la información sobre las reparaciones y cambió el titular, pero la publicación original ya se había compartido mucho en redes sociales.','The newspaper later added the repair information and changed its headline, but the original post had already been widely shared on social media.'],
['La redacción decidió publicar la corrección en las mismas cuentas, en lugar de modificar en silencio solamente el texto de su página.','The editors decided to publish the correction on the same accounts rather than silently modifying only the website text.'],
['Para la siguiente evaluación se propuso comparar semanas parecidas, tomar en cuenta los horarios y preguntar también a quienes no eran visitantes frecuentes.','The next evaluation would compare similar weeks, account for opening hours and also ask people who were not frequent visitors.'],
['La conclusión más precisa era más prudente, pero también más útil: la sala se estaba usando y su efecto específico todavía requería mejores datos.','The more precise conclusion was more cautious but useful: the room was being used, while its specific effect still required better data.']]]],
['A true count does not automatically support the headline’s causal claim.','A fair comparison needs comparable access and opening hours.','Positive experiences and weak causal evidence can coexist.','A correction should reach the audience that saw the original claim.']],
['C1-academic','Two explanations for an apparent improvement','analytical case study',
[
['The question behind the result',[
['Un equipo universitario quería averiguar si ampliar el horario de la biblioteca ayudaba a que el alumnado participara con mayor regularidad en grupos de estudio independiente.','A university team wanted to establish whether extending library hours helped students attend independent study groups more regularly.'],
['Al terminar un semestre aumentó la asistencia a los grupos nocturnos, pero Elena, autora del informe, se negó a presentar de inmediato ese cambio como un efecto del nuevo horario.','At the end of a semester evening-group attendance rose, but report author Elena refused to immediately present this as an effect of the new schedule.'],
['Durante el mismo semestre había cambiado el procedimiento de entrega de tareas: algunos trabajos tenían que discutirse primero entre estudiantes y después enviarse a la persona docente.','The assignment submission procedure changed that semester too: some work had to be discussed among students before being sent to a lecturer.'],
['Había que distinguir, por tanto, entre un horario que facilitaba la participación y una nueva exigencia que aumentaba el incentivo para participar en primer lugar.','It was therefore necessary to distinguish a schedule making participation easier from a new requirement increasing the incentive to participate at all.']]],
['What the comparisons could show',[
['El equipo comparó estudiantes de distintas carreras, aunque pronto reconoció que las diferencias entre ellas no se reducían a la posibilidad de usar la biblioteca.','The team compared students on different programmes but soon recognised that differences were not limited to library access.'],
['En una carrera había más personas que trabajaban de noche; en otra, más tareas colectivas obligatorias, y tampoco eran iguales los costos de traslado.','One programme had more people working evenings, another more compulsory group assignments, and travel costs were unequal too.'],
['Comparar promedios permitía describir una diferencia, pero no identificar qué parte dependía del horario y cuál de esas otras condiciones.','Comparing averages described a difference but did not identify how much depended on the schedule and how much on other conditions.'],
['En vez de buscar una cifra cómoda que cerrara la discusión, Elena propuso registrar las explicaciones alternativas y precisar qué observaciones adicionales permitirían distinguirlas.','Rather than seeking a convenient number to end the discussion, Elena proposed recording alternative explanations and specifying additional observations that could distinguish them.']]],
['The interview that complicated the average',[
['En las entrevistas, varias personas dijeron que por fin podían usar la biblioteca, aun cuando su frecuencia total de visitas casi no había cambiado durante el semestre.','In interviews several people said they could finally use the library, although their total visit frequency had barely changed that semester.'],
['Antes iban menos veces y se quedaban mucho tiempo; ahora podían elegir reuniones más breves, compatibles con el trabajo y las responsabilidades familiares.','Previously they visited less often and stayed a long time; now they could choose shorter meetings compatible with work and family responsibilities.'],
['Otras reconocieron que asistían principalmente porque la discusión colectiva se había incorporado a la tarea y que, sin esa exigencia, el horario ampliado no habría modificado su conducta.','Others acknowledged attending mainly because group discussion had become part of the assignment; without that requirement, extended hours would not have changed their behaviour.'],
['Estos relatos no sustituían los datos cuantitativos, pero mostraban que un mismo indicador podía ocultar experiencias distintas y mecanismos diferentes.','These accounts did not replace quantitative data, but showed that one indicator could conceal different experiences and mechanisms.']]],
['A recommendation within the evidence',[
['La recomendación final proponía mantener algunas horas nocturnas el siguiente semestre y recoger de manera sistemática información sobre acceso, tareas y motivos de participación.','The final recommendation proposed retaining some evening hours next semester and systematically collecting information about access, assignments and reasons for attending.'],
['No prometía que el horario, por sí solo, mejoraría los resultados del aprendizaje, pero tampoco concluía que los cambios observados carecieran de valor.','It did not promise that the schedule alone would improve learning outcomes, but neither did it conclude that observed changes had no value.'],
['La decisión respondía a una necesidad práctica visible; su revisión dependería de preguntas definidas de antemano y no únicamente de una medida general de satisfacción.','The decision addressed a visible practical need; review would depend on questions defined beforehand, not just a general satisfaction measure.'],
['Elena insistió en que una conclusión cautelosa no representaba un fracaso: permitía actuar sin aparentar un conocimiento mayor que el respaldado por el material disponible.','Elena insisted that a cautious conclusion was not a failure: it allowed action without pretending to know more than the available material supported.']]]],
['Separate easier access from a stronger incentive to attend.','A comparison can describe differences without isolating their cause.','An unchanged average may conceal a meaningful change in experience.','A provisional decision can be useful without an unsupported causal promise.']],
['C2-science','What the trial did not promise','qualified public explanation',
[
['A sentence that travelled',[
['En un proyecto de monitoreo ambiental de una ciudad ficticia se probaron nuevos sensores de temperatura del río, y una presentación pública afirmó que el sistema permitía detectar los cambios con mayor rapidez.','In a fictional city’s environmental monitoring project, new river-temperature sensors were trialled, and a public presentation said the system enabled changes to be detected sooner.'],
['El informe técnico vinculaba esa afirmación con condiciones específicas de la prueba; una síntesis posterior, en cambio, la convirtió en la promesa de que el río estaría vigilado de forma continua y confiable.','The technical report tied that statement to particular trial conditions; a later summary instead turned it into a promise of continuous, reliable monitoring.'],
['La diferencia sólo parecía menor mientras nadie preguntara qué entendería razonablemente el público por continuo ni quién tendría que responder cuando no llegara un aviso.','The difference seemed minor only while nobody asked what the public would reasonably understand by continuous or who would answer when no alert arrived.'],
['La editora no suponía que hubiera una intención de engañar: al abreviar el documento, el autor de la síntesis había eliminado una condición de validez, no un detalle accesorio.','The editor did not assume an intention to deceive: in shortening the document, the summary’s author had removed a condition of validity rather than an incidental detail.']]],
['The gaps in the record',[
['Se programaron cien mediciones durante la prueba: noventa y cuatro llegaron a tiempo y seis no alcanzaron la base de datos debido a una interrupción de la conexión.','One hundred measurements were scheduled during the trial: ninety-four arrived on time and six did not reach the database because connectivity was interrupted.'],
['Los registros recibidos permitían evaluar los momentos para los que había información, pero los ausentes no confirmaban ni la estabilidad de la temperatura ni un cambio repentino.','The received records allowed evaluation of moments for which information existed; missing records confirmed neither stable temperature nor a sudden change.'],
['Recuperar después parte de esos registros no borraba la limitación, porque la promesa no se refería sólo a conocer eventualmente un resultado, sino a disponer de él a tiempo.','Recovering some records later did not remove the limitation: the promise concerned not merely eventually knowing a result but having it in time.'],
['Afirmar que funcionó la mayoría de los dispositivos no equivalía, por tanto, a afirmar que el monitoreo fue ininterrumpido, aunque ambas formulaciones pudieran sonar parecidas en una conversación pública.','Saying that most devices worked was therefore not equivalent to saying monitoring was uninterrupted, although the two formulations might sound similar in public discussion.']]],
['Two objections that deserved different answers',[
['Una representante vecinal dudaba de que tuviera sentido continuar sin garantizar la transmisión ininterrumpida, mientras que el responsable del proyecto temía que enumerar las limitaciones ocultara el avance conseguido.','A residents’ representative doubted the point of continuing without guaranteed uninterrupted transmission, while the project lead feared listing limitations would hide progress.'],
['La editora propuso no confundir las dos inquietudes: una se refería al nivel de servicio aceptable y la otra a cómo comunicarlo sin perder exactitud ni relevancia.','The editor proposed not confusing these concerns: one concerned an acceptable service level and the other how to communicate it without losing accuracy or relevance.'],
['El avance podía ser real y, a la vez, insuficiente para un uso determinado; reconocer lo segundo no obligaba a negar lo primero ni a callar a quién le resultaba útil el sistema.','Progress could be real yet insufficient for a particular use; recognising the latter did not require denying the former or concealing who benefited.'],
['Sin embargo, hablar de beneficios no podía sustituir la explicación de cómo se marcarían los vacíos, quién revisaría las alertas y qué conclusiones no era válido sacar del silencio.','But speaking of benefits could not replace explaining how gaps would be marked, who would review alerts and what conclusions could not validly be drawn from silence.']]],
['A shorter explanation that kept its limits',[
['La nueva síntesis pública explicó que, bajo las condiciones de la prueba, el sistema aportó más observaciones oportunas, aunque algunas transmisiones fallaron y la ausencia de avisos no demostraba que nada hubiera cambiado.','The revised public summary explained that the system provided more timely observations under trial conditions, but some transmissions failed and no alerts did not prove nothing changed.'],
['Se conservó una tabla separada de registros recibidos, tardíos y ausentes para el personal técnico; al vecindario se le indicó dónde consultar el estado de la conexión y a quién comunicar discrepancias.','A separate table of received, late and missing records remained for technical staff; residents were told where to see connection status and whom to notify of discrepancies.'],
['Continuar la prueba quedó ligado a una acción verificable: ensayar un medio de transmisión de respaldo antes de ampliar la red y definir por anticipado cómo se evaluarían los retrasos.','Continuing the trial was tied to a verifiable action: test backup transmission before expanding the network and define beforehand how delays would be evaluated.'],
['La incertidumbre siguió siendo visible, sin convertirse en pretexto para posponerlo todo ni en una reserva conveniente que permitiera justificar cualquier resultado una vez conocido.','Uncertainty remained visible without becoming a pretext for postponing everything or a convenient caveat to justify any result once known.']]]],
['Preserve a condition that limits what the original claim warrants.','Missing or late data cannot be treated as timely evidence of stability.','Separate fitness for a purpose from how its limits should be communicated.','State a reviewable next step without promising certainty.']]
];
const questions={
 'B1-community':[
 ['Why did the first plan need more than a new location?',['The entrance and communication also needed attention','The books had all disappeared','The school had cancelled every event'],0,[1,2],'The delay could be explained, but visitors also needed a usable route to the hall.'],
 ['How did the narrator’s idea of useful work change?',['Only tasks listed first were important','Responding to people could take priority over the list','Counting books became unnecessary'],1,[0,2],'The initial detailed plan was revised when volunteers discovered practical access needs.'],
 ['Why was the event not judged only by the book total?',['The organisers could not count','All visitors bought the same number of books','New connections and requests for another event also mattered'],2,[0,3],'Compare the original exchange purpose with participants’ later comments.'],
 ['Which next plan follows the whole account?',['Keep a clear plan, check access and keys, and explain the rain arrangement','Cancel whenever a problem appears','Publish only a place and starting time again'],0,[1,2,3],'The final plan keeps preparation while learning from delay, access and communication problems.']],
 'B2-media':[
 ['What does the text challenge about the first headline?',['Whether anybody used the room','Whether the increase can be attributed to the new room alone','Whether the director spoke at all'],1,[0,1],'The count and visible use can be real while the causal explanation remains weak.'],
 ['Why do repairs and longer hours matter together?',['They prove the room has no value','They cancel out automatically','They change the opportunity to visit in the compared periods'],2,[1,3],'A comparison of totals needs comparable access and exposure time.'],
 ['How can both the director and the reader have a useful point?',['Experience supports demand, while the comparison does not isolate a cause','Their statements mean exactly the same thing','Only numerical evidence can ever be useful'],0,[1,2],'A practical need and a weak causal claim are different issues.'],
 ['Why publish the correction on the original social accounts?',['To avoid explaining the repairs','To reach people who received the earlier claim','To erase all positive comments'],1,[0,3],'Changing the website alone may miss the audience reached by the original post.']],
 'C1-academic':[
 ['Which two explanations need to be kept separate?',['Student age and the building colour','Access made easier and an incentive strengthened by new assignments','Averages and interviews as identical evidence'],1,[0,2],'The schedule and assignment requirement could act through different mechanisms.'],
 ['What limits the comparison between programmes?',['Programmes differ only in names','Every student has identical travel costs','Work, assignments and travel conditions differ as well'],2,[0,1],'The comparison describes differences without isolating the schedule’s contribution.'],
 ['Why can an almost unchanged visit frequency still matter?',['The pattern and practical accessibility of visits may have improved','All interviews replace numerical records','A stable average proves the schedule caused every improvement'],0,[1,2],'The accounts reveal changes in experience hidden by a broad indicator.'],
 ['Which recommendation stays within the evidence?',['Promise better learning outcomes from the hours alone','Retain some hours provisionally and collect evidence to distinguish explanations','Stop collecting evidence because a decision is needed'],1,[0,3],'Practical action can be provisional and linked to specified review questions.']],
 'C2-science':[
 ['What was lost when the technical statement became a public promise?',['The existence of a river','The conditions limiting the original claim','Every mention of a possible benefit'],1,[0,3],'A condition of validity was removed, broadening what a reader would reasonably expect.'],
 ['Why do later recovered records not fulfil the original promise?',['Recovered data can never be useful','The missing records prove stable temperatures','The promise concerned timely information as well as eventual information'],2,[0,1],'Distinguish eventual availability from uninterrupted and timely monitoring.'],
 ['How should the two objections be handled?',['Separate fitness for an intended use from how limitations are communicated','Treat every concern as evidence against all progress','Explain benefits instead of addressing missing records'],0,[1,2],'Progress and insufficient fitness for a particular purpose can coexist.'],
 ['What makes the final qualification useful rather than an excuse?',['It permits any later outcome to count as success','It preserves limits and names an action and review condition','It avoids naming any remaining uncertainty'],1,[2,3],'Backup testing and a predefined treatment of delay make the next step reviewable.']]
};
const units={};
const examples=lt?{
 'B1-community':['Pirma knygų šventė → reikia aiškaus plano.','First book event: the narrator wants a clear plan.'],
 'B2-media':['Antraštė: trečdalio augimas pristatomas kaip neabejotina sėkmė.','The headline frames the one-third increase as unquestionable success.'],
 'C1-academic':['Klausimas: ar ilgesnis darbo laikas padeda reguliariau dalyvauti?','Research question: whether longer hours support more regular attendance.'],
 'C2-science':['Bandymas: nauji jutikliai → greičiau pastebimi pokyčiai.','Trial claim: new sensors allow changes to be noticed sooner.']
}:{
 'B1-community':['Primera feria → necesidad de un plan claro.','First book event: the narrator wants a clear plan.'],
 'B2-media':['Titular: un aumento de una tercera parte presentado como éxito indiscutible.','The headline frames the one-third increase as unquestionable success.'],
 'C1-academic':['Pregunta: ¿el horario ampliado facilita una participación más regular?','Research question: whether longer hours support more regular attendance.'],
 'C2-science':['Prueba: nuevos sensores → detección más rápida de cambios.','Trial claim: new sensors allow changes to be noticed sooner.']
};
for(const [id,title,genre,sections,sectionGuides] of rows){
 const band=id.split('-')[0];
 units[id]={id,band,title,genre,fictional:true,
  purpose:band==='B1'?'Brief a new volunteer on what happened and how to prepare next time.':band==='B2'?'Brief an editor on what the evidence supports and how to correct the public message.':band==='C1'?'Brief a study committee on two explanations, the limits of the comparison and a provisional decision.':'Brief a public communications team without losing the conditions that limit the technical claim.',
  strategy:band==='B1'?'Track events, reasons and changes across the four parts.':band==='B2'?'Separate a reported number, its comparison and the causal claim.':band==='C1'?'Keep alternative explanations and different evidence types distinct.':'Track what each qualification allows a reader to conclude and what it does not.',
  sections:sections.map(([title,lines],i)=>({id:'part-'+(i+1),title,lines,guide:sectionGuides[i]})),
  noteExample:{quote:sections[0][1][0][0],note:examples[id][0],meaning:examples[id][1]},
  questions:questions[id].map(([prompt,options,answer,sections,explanation])=>({prompt,options,answer,sections,explanation})),
  noteTeaching:['Choose notes for the reader’s purpose; do not copy every sentence.','For each part, keep a useful point in the target language and a short exact source quotation that supports it.','Use the notes to draft the brief. Distinguish facts, interpretations and the proposed next step.'],
  goals:band==='B1'?['Explain the sequence and the reasons for two changes.','Use details from different parts to explain the final judgement.','Give a practical next step for the volunteer.']:band==='B2'?['Distinguish the count from the causal interpretation.','Represent the useful points on both sides.','Recommend a correction and a fairer next comparison.']:band==='C1'?['Keep the two mechanisms separate.','Explain what the comparison and interviews can each support.','Recommend a provisional action and specified evidence for review.']:['Preserve conditions, timing distinctions and uncertainty.','Represent both objections without merging their purposes.','Give an audience-appropriate next step with a reviewable condition.'],
  practiceRange:band==='B1'?[110,170]:band==='B2'?[150,220]:band==='C1'?[180,270]:[200,300]
 };
 const plans=window.WordamiLearningDesign?.units[id];
 if(plans){for(const skill of ['reading','mediation','writing'])plans.outcomes[skill].relatedPracticeIds=[...(plans.outcomes[skill].relatedPracticeIds||[]),'extended.'+id+'.'+skill];}
}
window.WordamiExtendedReadingContent=Object.freeze({version:1,scope:'Prepared longer texts, purposeful notes and self-reviewed source-based briefs; no independent proficiency grade',units});
})();
